      "headline": "A city read at two scales",
      "body": "<h3>The monumental core is a strong orientation framework.</h3><p>The Mall, the Potomac edge and distinctive civic buildings provide large-scale references. Smaller streets, façades and local public spaces establish the neighbourhood-scale experience.</p><p>Washington’s clear overall composition therefore coexists with different local identities. The atlas’s findings concern physical form and documented history; they do not claim that all residents perceive the city alike.</p>",
