      "headline": "The plan evolved through implementation",
      "body": "<h3>The capital is a layered project.</h3><p>The 1790 Residence Act established the federal seat. L’Enfant’s 1791 plan set out the grid, diagonal avenues and civic sites; Ellicott revised and published the plan in 1792. The government moved to Washington in 1800.</p><p>Nineteenth-century building and landscape changes altered the original proposal. The 1901–1902 McMillan Commission reasserted a formal monumental landscape, followed by decades of implementation.</p>",
